@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+---
+id: task-001-give-each-task-a-stable-unique-id
+type: task
+title: "Give each task a stable, unique id"
+status: pending
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Give each task a unique identifier that keeps working after the task is renamed: `add` returns a task
+with an `id`, the list gets a `get(id)` method, and `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`,
+`untag` and `remove` accept a task's id as well as its title.
+
+## What I did
+
+- `src/domain/task.ts`: added `id: string` to `Task`; `createTask(id, input)` now takes the id as a
+  parameter instead of deriving it itself, so `task.ts` stays free of state.
+- `src/domain/list.ts`: the list keeps its `Map` keyed by `id` instead of by title, and assigns ids from
+  a private, monotonically increasing counter (`nextId`, stringified) — no clock or randomness, per the
+  `r3-no-clock-or-randomness` directive. Added `get(id)`. `find` and the methods built on it now resolve
+  their argument as an id first, then as a title, so every existing method accepts either. Duplicate-title
+  and rename-collision checks now scan by title (`byTitle`) since the map key is no longer the title.
+- `test/list.test.ts`: added tests for a unique id on `add`, `get` by id (including the not-found case),
+  and an id surviving a `rename` and staying usable afterwards; updated the existing "adds an open task"
+  test to allow for the new `id` field.
+
+All 8 tests pass (`npm test`).
